ate_accruals":-0.025377591525236262,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":29.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.06780772386930893,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":94.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.001776599249038835,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.0030878321257596583,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.07939035830684485,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":86.8,"_gate_incr_roic":0.036414870465680316,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":28.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.035471476272862235,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":21.5,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06084319430123131,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":15.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.028973560807791232,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":39.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.0593434192429588,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":59.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.039459086922504494,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03144627858491433,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":10.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0031358647487899653,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00174,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Xcel Energy Inc., through its subsidiaries, operates as an electric and natural gas delivery company in the United States. It operates through Regulated Electric Utility and Regulated Natural Gas Utility segments. The company generates, purchases, transmits, distributes, and sells electricity through its energy portfolio, including wind, nuclear, hydroelectric, biomass, and solar power from both owned generation facilities and PPAs, as well as its fossil fuel energy portfolio, such as coal and natural gas; sale and resale of wholesale transmission service; and engages in wholesale commodity and trading operations. It also purchases, transports, stores, distributes, and sells natural gas; develops and leases natural gas pipelines and storage facilities; operates interstate natural gas pipeline; and invests in rental housing projects, energy technology companies, and community solar garden nonregulated assets. It serves electric and natural gas customers in portions of Colorado, Michigan, Minnesota, New Mexico, North Dakota, South Dakota, Texas, and Wisconsin. The company was formerly known as Northern States Power company. Xcel Energy Inc. was incorporated in 1909 and is headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert C. Frenzel | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 54 | Compensation: $4.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the above the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Xcel Energy Inc. is a large-cap utilities business with a $52.4B market cap on $14.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $6.8B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 3.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 51% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5135161480554701},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Regulatory rate-case risk and rising cost of capital \u2014 the allowed return is set by commissions, and the business lives or dies by that negotiation.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Grid modernisation capex burden \u2014 aging infrastructure requires massive reinvestment that regulators may not fully allow into rate base, compressing earned returns.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","41 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why the data center slowdown concern is overblown. Two stocks to buy amid the fear","source":"cnbc.com","link":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/13/data-center-slowdown-utility-stocks.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":179458